    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d932">

                <pb facs="0977" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7331A15/26</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary to the President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Akerson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-14">November 14, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Akerson</hi>: The Department has been
                    informed that within a week or ten days the All America Cables Company will take
                    over the operation of the cable system of Venezuela and this Company has
                    requested that at that time the President send a message of greeting to the
                    President of Venezuela.</p>
                <p>You will recall that in the past upon the occasion of the opening of direct
                    communication systems between the United States and various other countries
                    notably Hungary, Cuba, and Spain, the President has been good enough to send
                    such a message.</p>
                <p>I therefore transmit herewith a copy of a communication which I should recommend
                    be sent if the President approves. I shall be pleased to have this message sent
                    to the President of Venezuela at the appropriate time, if the President so
                    desires.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis White</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d932-a1.xml" xpointer="d932-a1"/>
            </div>
